        [31m`Add it to ENVIRONMENTS in config.js.`[39m
      );
    }
    [34mreturn[39m settings;
  }

  [34mconst[39m APP_SETTINGS = [33mresolveSettings[39m(window.location.hostname);

  The staging and local hosts are placeholders for you to replace. The production endpoint is the existing
  [38;5;153mhttps://api.example.com/login[39m, carried over unchanged, so behavior on the real host is identical to today.

  [1mData flow:[0m [38;5;153mconfig.js[39m runs first, resolves once at load, and publishes [38;5;153mAPP_SETTINGS[39m. [38;5;153mapp.js[39m reads
  [38;5;153mAPP_SETTINGS.apiEndpoint[39m at the point of use. Resolution is eager and happens once — no lazy lookup, nothing to
  re-resolve.

  [1mError handling:[0m an unrecognized hostname throws during [38;5;153mconfig.js[39m, before [38;5;153mapp.js[39m parses. Concretely that means the
  submit listener is never attached, so the form silently does nothing while the console shows an error naming the
  hostname. That's the loud failure you chose, but it's worth being explicit that "loud" here means "console error plus
  a dead form," not a visible message to the user. Adding user-facing error UI is out of scope unless you want it.

  [1mTesting:[0m this repo has no test runner, no lint config, and no CI, so there's no established pattern to follow and I
  don't plan to add one as part of this. [38;5;153mresolveSettings[39m is a pure function specifically so a test is a one-liner
  whenever you do add a runner. Verification for this change is manual: open [38;5;153mindex.html[39m from disk and confirm the
  console shows no error and [38;5;153mAPP_SETTINGS.apiEndpoint[39m is the localhost value; then temporarily add an unmapped hostname
  case to confirm the throw message reads well. I can set up a minimal test runner instead if you want one — that's a
  separate decision, not something I'll fold in silently.

  [1mExplicitly out of scope:[0m [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m and [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m (not loaded by the page), any change to [38;5;153mlogin()[39m actually making
  a network call, and any build tooling.

  Does this look right? Once you approve, I'll write it up as a spec at
  [38;5;153mdocs/hyperpowers/specs/2026-09-26-settings-module-design.md[39m (uncommitted), run it past the Codex spec gate, and hand
  you the spec to review before any code gets written.

